<title>USA: Montell may issue $750 mln in 144A debt - US sources.</title>
<headline>Montell may issue $750 mln in 144A debt - US sources.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Montell Polyolefins NV is expected to tap the U.S. corporate bond primary market with a $750 debt offering via the private placement market, syndicate sources said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Montell NV is a 50/50 plastics joint venture between Royal Dutch/Shell and Italy's Montedison.</p>
<p>The deal, which is expected to price on Wednesday, includes $500 million in 10-year 144A notes and $250 million in 30-year 144A notes, sources said.</p>
<p>The offering is expected to be underwritten by Morgan Stanley &amp; Co Inc.</p>
<p>(( --Nancy Leinfuss, 212-859-1675 ))</p>
